# Scratch-file patterns are ANCHORED with a leading slash. A pattern with no
# slash matches at ANY depth: a bare junit.xml in a product .gitignore
# silently excluded a required committed fixture in P060 of this mission, and
# a cold clone then failed with 17 failures and 9 errors while every local
# check passed.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
/build/
/dist/
/.venv/
/venv/
/.pytest_cache/
/.hypothesis/
/.ruff_cache/
/.coverage
/htmlcov/
/junit.xml
/.config/
# This product serialises NO model: the predictor is refitted from the
# committed record by every script that needs it, which is why the
# scikit-learn ceiling in pyproject.toml is about the numbers and not about a
# pickle format. These patterns exist so a future change cannot add one
# silently and leave the ceiling reading as merely advisory.
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.joblib
*.pkl
# The committed per-pass record, its manifest and the generator's transcript
# are evidence and must reach a cold clone. Listed as negations so that a
# future broad pattern cannot swallow them silently.
!/data/passes.csv
!/data/manifest.json
!/data/generate_passes.py
!/data/generate_passes_output.txt
# Every validation script's raw output is evidence and must ship.
!/validation/*_output.txt
